      "claim": "A parent reports that strangers can send messages and friend requests to a child, and these cannot be disabled.",
      "stance": "risk",
      "quote": "other users can send messages and friend requests although these are audited for language as appropriate to the age of the player is important to ensure that unwanted interactions with strangers are not occurring along with the usual advice to play games together with younger players and keep them in shared family spaces there are some good parenting controls on roblox that ensure your child has an appropriate experience the first thing to ensure is that you entered their age correctly so that the appropriate safe chat mode is applied to their accounts however it's important to know that the specified age doesn't filter the content in the games all players can access all the games regardless of their age"
    },
    {
      "ref": "[D530]",
      "area": "money",
      "claim": "A parent reports that Roblox incentivizes children to spend money on in-app purchases to buy gear, vehicles, or advance faster.",
      "stance": "risk",
      "quote": "finally although roblox is free-to-play there are in-app purchases in the game to buy extra gear and extra vehicles or advance more quickly children are incentivized to pay for these and to ask for more roblox money so it is important that you set up the appropriate passwords on any credit cards associated with your account"
